  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "The final rules satisfy all four red lines: S2 gives per-model results to customers and regulators but not the general public, S3 sets a 72-month retrofit, and S4 sets 36 months for built-in suppression. However, S2's permanent 7% failure limit with corrective action above 5% is weaker than the 5% safe/acceptable standard and protects Northwind's Hearth 10. S5's mandatory 8/100k recall trigger will force a recall for Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k), while Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4/100k) stays below it."
